.TH CJSON_DICTIONARY_REMOVE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cjson_dictionary_remove \- remove and free a key from an object node
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cjson.h>

ccol_retval_t cjson_dictionary_remove(cjson obj, const char *key);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Removes the member with the given key from the object node obj and
frees its value together with everything below it.  The remaining
members keep their order.

A walk with cjson_dictionary_first(3) and cjson_dictionary_next(3)
may remove the member that its cursor stands on, for example with
cjson_dictionary_remove(obj, it.key), and then go on.  Removing the
member after it, the one the cursor reads next, invalidates the
cursor, but removing any other member doesn't.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success        - the member was removed and freed.
ccol_invalid_args   - obj or key is NULL, or obj is not a CJSON_DICTIONARY.
ccol_key_not_found  - the object has no such key.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cjson_dictionary_set (3),
.BR cjson_dictionary_get (3),
.BR cjson_dictionary_first (3),
.BR cjson_list_remove (3)
